---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout lang="en">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Cybersecurity · systems · understanding</p>
    <h1>Builder. Explorer. Cybersecurity.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I work in cybersecurity. When something looks unnecessarily complex,
      I strip away terminology, trace components, data, identities,
      trust boundaries and assumptions — and rebuild the problem from there.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <article>
      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p>Technical articles and notes, wherever they happen to be published.</p>
      <a href="/en/writing/">Read →</a>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <p>Repositories, tools and things built over the years.</p>
      <a href="/en/projects/">Explore →</a>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>Some professional context. Not a brochure.</p>
      <a href="/en/about/">About me →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="note">
    <p>The goal is simple: reach the end and think <strong>“I get it.”</strong></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
